{"name":"Hulett Ore","hex":"#726f6c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ore","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Orejón."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Rock or other material that contains valuable or utilitarian materials; primarily a rock containing metals or gems for which it is typically mined and processed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ore"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hulett","blocks":[{"text":"The Hulett was an ore unloader that was widely used on the Great Lakes of North America. It was unsuited to tidewater ports because it could not adjust for rising and falling tides, although one was used in New York City."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Huletts.jpg/330px-Huletts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hulett","wikidata":"Q12060591"},{"title":"Ore","blocks":[{"text":"Ore is natural rock or sediment that contains one or more valuable minerals, typically including metals, concentrated above background levels, and that is economically viable to mine and process. Ore grade refers to the concentration of the desired material it contains. The value of the metals or minerals a rock contains must be weighed against the cost of extraction to determine whether it is of sufficiently high grade to be worth mining and is therefore considered an ore. A complex ore is one containing more than one valuable mineral."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Banded_iron_formation.png/330px-Banded_iron_formation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ore","wikidata":"Q102798"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Hulett-bucket.jpg/500px-Hulett-bucket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Hulett-bucket.jpg/500px-Hulett-bucket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Hulett's bucket in the foreground, while another scoops ore from the hold. The operator's cab is in the leg, behind the aperture above the bucket and below the circular sprocket.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHulett-bucket.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Hulett-discharging.jpg/500px-Hulett-discharging.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Hulett-discharging.jpg/500px-Hulett-discharging.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Discharging the travelling hopper's load into a waiting hopper car.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHulett-discharging.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Huletts_P6290296.JPG/120px-Huletts_P6290296.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Huletts_P6290296.JPG/250px-Huletts_P6290296.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Huletts_P6290296.JPG/120px-Huletts_P6290296.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHuletts_P6290296.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Huletts_P6290297.JPG/120px-Huletts_P6290297.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Huletts_P6290297.JPG/250px-Huletts_P6290297.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Hule